{
  "description": "The image shows a single quadrupedal animal standing in right-facing profile on a small patch of dirt with a few pebbles, dry leaves and tufts of grass. Its overall body proportions, head shape, legs and hooves are those of a horse or pony, with short brown fur on the head, lower legs and underparts and a lighter tan or off-white color on the muzzle, throat, chest and belly. Most of the dorsal and lateral surfaces including the back, sides, neck, forehead, upper portions of all four legs, and the long thick tapering tail are densely covered in overlapping brown keratinous scales with lighter tan edges arranged in diagonal rows, resembling a pangolin. The scales form a crest along the dorsal midline of the neck where a mane would be and a cap over the forehead between the ears. The head is horse-like with a dark eye, large nostril, closed mouth with whiskers, and two upright pointed ears. The lower legs are furry and end in solid rounded hooves. No wings, horns, or additional appendages are visible.",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "head",
      "looks_like": "horse-like head in right profile with brown fur, a dark eye with eyelid, a large nostril, a closed muzzle with light tan around the mouth and chin and small whiskers, and a cap of overlapping scales on the forehead and crown",
      "where": "at the far right end of the body, facing right, attached to the neck"
    },
    {
      "part": "ears",
      "looks_like": "two upright pointed horse ears with brown outer fur and darker inner fur, triangular with rounded tips",
      "where": "on top of the head, one slightly behind the other due to profile view, above and behind the eye"
    },
    {
      "part": "mane",
      "looks_like": "not hair but a crest of large overlapping brown scales with tan edges, forming a mane-like ridge",
      "where": "along the dorsal midline of the neck from just behind the ears to the shoulders"
    },
    {
      "part": "legs",
      "looks_like": "four sturdy horse-like legs, upper portions covered in overlapping brown scales, lower portions with short brown fur and slightly shaggy fetlocks",
      "where": "under the trunk, two forelegs under the chest and two hindlegs under the hips, supporting the body"
    },
    {
      "part": "feet",
      "looks_like": "four solid rounded ungulate hooves, dark brown with a lighter coronet band at the top",
      "where": "at the distal end of each leg, in contact with the ground"
    },
    {
      "part": "tail",
      "looks_like": "a long thick tapering tail entirely covered in overlapping brown scales arranged in encircling rows, pointed at the tip",
      "where": "at the left rear of the body extending from the rump and hanging down almost to the ground"
    },
    {
      "part": "scales",
      "looks_like": "numerous overlapping leaf-shaped keratinous scales in dark to medium brown with lighter tan edges and a central ridge, arranged in neat diagonal rows",
      "where": "covering the back, sides, neck, forehead cap, upper forelegs and hindlegs, and the entire tail, leaving only the face, lower legs, belly, chest and throat with fur"
    },
    {
      "part": "plates",
      "looks_like": "the same overlapping armor plates as the scales, large and scale-like with a keeled shape",
      "where": "forming the continuous armor over the trunk, neck, head cap, upper legs and tail"
    },
    {
      "part": "markings",
      "looks_like": "lighter tan to off-white shaggy fur on the ventral belly, chest and throat contrasting with the darker brown fur of the head and lower legs",
      "where": "on the underside of the body between the legs and along the lower neck and chest"
    }
  ],
